  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 810.02 Groundwater Monitoring and Treatment Violations",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 810.02 Groundwater Monitoring and Treatment Violations. The statement required by Env-Dw 801.03(a)(3) to describe groundwater monitoring and treatment technique violations shall read as follows:\n\n“Inadequately treated or inadequately protected water may contain disease-causing organisms. These organisms can cause symptoms such as diarrhea, nausea, cramps, and associated headaches.”\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Dw 800) #9730, eff 6-30-10; ss by #12675, eff 1-1-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw800.html"
